      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product.",
      "worked_solution": "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $‖v‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\cdot (2\\cdot 2)+3\\cdot 3+2\\cdot (4\\cdot 4)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8+9+32} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
